---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import ParticipationCoalitionScenarios from './ParticipationCoalitionScenarios.astro';
import ParticipationEstimatedCoalitions from './ParticipationEstimatedCoalitions.astro';
import ParticipationDemographicCounts from './ParticipationDemographicCounts.astro';
const base = '/participation-survey/20261107-02/';
type JointRow = { prior_choice_share_pct: number | null;
	current_choice_pct_within_prior_choice: Record<string, number | null> | null };
type Table = { state_code: string; contest_code: string; contest_title?: string;
	subset: { sub: number; longName: string }; status: string; source_timestamp?: string;
	source_url?: string; source_reported_respondents?: number;
	joint_question_rows?: Record<string, JointRow>;
	arithmetic_from_rounded_percentages_per_100_current_group_voters?: Record<string, number> };
type Jurisdiction = { state_code: string; reviewed_joint_tables: number };
const review: { tables: Table[]; jurisdictions: Jurisdiction[] } = JSON.parse(
	readFileSync(`public${base}joint-table-review.json`, 'utf8'));
const states = ['US', ...review.jurisdictions.map(row => row.state_code)];
const names: Record<string, string> = {
	AL: 'Alabama', AK: 'Alaska', AZ: 'Arizona', AR: 'Arkansas', CA: 'California',
	CO: 'Colorado', CT: 'Connecticut', DE: 'Delaware', FL: 'Florida', GA: 'Georgia',
	HI: 'Hawaii', ID: 'Idaho', IL: 'Illinois', IN: 'Indiana', IA: 'Iowa',
	KS: 'Kansas', KY: 'Kentucky', LA: 'Louisiana', ME: 'Maine', MD: 'Maryland',
	MA: 'Massachusetts', MI: 'Michigan', MN: 'Minnesota', MS: 'Mississippi', MO: 'Missouri',
	MT: 'Montana', NE: 'Nebraska', NV: 'Nevada', NH: 'New Hampshire', NJ: 'New Jersey',
	NM: 'New Mexico', NY: 'New York', NC: 'North Carolina', ND: 'North Dakota', OH: 'Ohio',
	OK: 'Oklahoma', OR: 'Oregon', PA: 'Pennsylvania', RI: 'Rhode Island', SC: 'South Carolina',
	SD: 'South Dakota', TN: 'Tennessee', TX: 'Texas', UT: 'Utah', VT: 'Vermont',
	VA: 'Virginia', WA: 'Washington', WV: 'West Virginia', WI: 'Wisconsin', WY: 'Wyoming',
	DC: 'District of Columbia', US: 'National House',
};
const name = (code: string) => names[code];
const qualified = review.tables.filter(row => row.status === 'published_joint_question_reviewed');
const qualifiedStates = review.jurisdictions.filter(row => row.reviewed_joint_tables > 0).length;
const labels: Record<string, string> = {
	published_joint_question_reviewed: 'Rounded switching arithmetic reviewed',
	withheld_source_disabled: 'Disabled by publisher',
	withheld_source_not_acquired: 'Source not acquired',
	withheld_suppressed_switching_cell: 'Required cell suppressed',
	withheld_unreconciled_prior_composition: 'Prior composition does not reconcile',
	withheld_nonunique_literal_dem_rep_comparison: 'No unique literal D/R comparison',
	withheld_special_election_scope_review: 'Special-election scope review pending',
};
const pct = (value: number | null | undefined) => value == null ? 'Unavailable' : `${value}%`;
const mass = (row: Table, key: string) => {
	const value = row.arithmetic_from_rounded_percentages_per_100_current_group_voters?.[key];
	return value == null ? 'Withheld' : value.toFixed(2);
};
---

<section id="participation-survey" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="participation-survey-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">2024 to 2026 · Survey-reported switching and composition</p>
		<h2 id="participation-survey-title">What the current electorate reports</h2>
		<p>State and demographic joint tables from CNN's Voter Poll by SSRS.
			<strong>{qualified.length} qualified tables across {qualifiedStates} states and the national House poll</strong>;
			not nationwide population attribution. Expand a jurisdiction to compare each available office separately.
			These tables work without JavaScript.</p>
	</header>
	<p>Each conditional percentage is among the selected 2026 poll group's respondents who recalled that
		2024 presidential choice, <strong>not all of the original Trump or Harris coalition</strong>.
		The two mass columns are reported switchers per 100 members of the selected current poll group,
		calculated from rounded joint cells. They are not margin points or percentages of overall swing.</p>
	<p>Some unrecontacted respondents retain pre-election choices. This is not a validated record of individual
		ballots or causal persuasion. CNN, NBC and MS NOW use the same SSRS study, not independent samples.
		<strong>Population drop-off and design-aware subgroup confidence intervals remain unavailable.</strong></p>
	<p>The prior nonvote and other-choice columns describe each current poll group's recalled 2024
		presidential composition. They are not demographic turnout rates. A reported presidential nonvoter
		may have voted in another 2024 contest; these tables cannot distinguish first-time voters,
		returning voters or newly eligible residents.</p>
	<ParticipationDemographicCounts names={names} />
	<ParticipationEstimatedCoalitions names={names} />
	<ParticipationCoalitionScenarios names={names} />
	{states.map(code => {
		const tables = review.tables.filter(row => row.state_code === code);
		const contests = [...new Set(tables.map(row => row.contest_code))];
		return <details id={`survey-${code}`} class="explorer-notes" open={code === 'US'} data-survey-jurisdiction={code}>
			<summary>{name(code)} · {tables.filter(row =>
				row.status === 'published_joint_question_reviewed').length} qualified tables</summary>
			{tables.length === 0 && <p>No applicable candidate table is declared in this publisher's configuration.
				This is not a zero switching rate or evidence that other sources have no data.
				{code === 'DC' && ' D.C. was not sampled in this SSRS study.'}</p>}
			{contests.map(contest => {
				const rows = tables.filter(row => row.contest_code === contest);
				return <div data-survey-contest={contest}>
					<h3>{rows.find(row => row.contest_title)?.contest_title ?? contest}</h3>
					<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${name(code)} ${contest} survey switching`}>
						<table data-publication-class="unscaled-qualified-survey-shares"><caption>Conditional cells and masses have different denominators. Source cells can
							remain visible when mass arithmetic is withheld; see qualification.</caption>
							<thead><tr><th scope="col">Poll group</th><th scope="col">Trump to D<br />(within recalled Trump)</th>
								<th scope="col">Harris to R<br />(within recalled Harris)</th>
								<th scope="col">Trump to D<br />(per 100 current group)</th>
								<th scope="col">Harris to R<br />(per 100 current group)</th>
								<th scope="col">No 2024 presidential vote<br />(% of current group)</th>
								<th scope="col">Other 2024 presidential choice<br />(% of current group)</th>
								<th scope="col">Source base</th><th scope="col">Qualification / source clock</th></tr></thead>
							<tbody>{rows.map(row => <tr data-survey-status={row.status} data-survey-subset={row.subset.sub}>
								<th scope="row">{row.subset.longName}</th>
								<td>{pct(row.joint_question_rows?.R.current_choice_pct_within_prior_choice?.D)}</td>
								<td>{pct(row.joint_question_rows?.D.current_choice_pct_within_prior_choice?.R)}</td>
								<td>{mass(row, 'reported_trump_to_dem')}</td><td>{mass(row, 'reported_harris_to_rep')}</td>
								<td data-survey-prior-nonvoter-share>{pct(row.joint_question_rows?.N?.prior_choice_share_pct)}</td>
								<td data-survey-prior-other-share>{pct(row.joint_question_rows?.O?.prior_choice_share_pct)}</td>
								<td>{row.source_reported_respondents == null || row.source_reported_respondents < 0
									? 'Unavailable' : row.source_reported_respondents.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
								<td>{labels[row.status] ?? row.status}
									{row.source_url && <><br /><a href={row.source_url}>Native source</a></>}
									{row.source_timestamp && <><br /><time>{row.source_timestamp}</time></>}</td>
							</tr>)}</tbody>
						</table>
					</div>
				</div>;
			})}
		</details>;
	})}
	<p class="caption">Groups overlap and must not be added. Native suppressed values stay unavailable;
		they are not zero. Composition shortfalls are preserved, not renormalized. Independent candidates
		and ambiguous major-party or special-election comparisons are not forced into ordinary D/R estimates.
		Source bases are not effective prior-choice-cell samples. Prior presidential nonvoting is not
		validated nonparticipation in every 2024 contest. No state estimate is allocated to counties or precincts.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Why population-scaled historical transitions are withheld</summary>
		<p>The <a href="/participation-publication-decision/20261107-01/decision.json">historical evidence decision for all 51 jurisdictions</a>
			preserves denominator-labeled survey shares, provider Initial Estimates and source observations.
			Original-coalition returning, switching and apparent-absence quantities are withheld because
			our candidate-cohort method has not passed population validation in any jurisdiction.</p>
		<p>Apparent absence is not measured staying home. Missing history is not nonvoting, prior presidential
			nonvote is not never voted, and new registration is not first-time voting. Complete frozen
			calculation archives remain available for reproducibility, not as supported population estimates.</p>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete survey tables + inputs + code (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${base}joint-table-review.json`} download>All reviewed cells and withholding reasons (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>Archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
		<a href="https://ssrs.com/wp-content/uploads/The-Voter-Poll-by-SSRS-Methodology-Statement_Final.pdf">SSRS methods</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-survey { min-width: 0; }
	#participation-survey details { margin-block: 0.8rem; }
	#participation-survey th, #participation-survey td { vertical-align: top; }
	#participation-survey time { font-size: 0.75rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
	#participation-survey summary { cursor: pointer; }
</style>
